<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Istanbul</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Istanbul is the city on the Bosporus formerly known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, taken by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in 1453. It became the capital of the Ottoman Empire and one of the largest and most cosmopolitan cities of the world. It remained the imperial centre until the empire's end after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/istanbul.jpg" alt="Istanbul" width="320" height="155" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hunanuk · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Historical_peninsula_and_modern_skyline_of_Istanbul.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
